# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b4), edited. jean_myriel's first conversation.

~ start
set jean_myriel_met
Narrator: Heat rolls from the hearth, smelling of quenched iron and coal smoke. The squat smith checks the edge of his neatly trimmed beard in a polished buckler.
jean_myriel [smile]: Step in out of the damp, strangers. Whether you need a mule shod, a blade silvered, or a bit of gold twisted pretty, my anvil is hot.
-> menu

~ menu
jean_myriel [neutral]: What can I hammer out for you today?
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask how he came to settle in Wickermoor -> work
* Ask about the mood in the village -> village
* [Arcana DC 14] Inspect the dark red patina inside his fuller-grooves -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
jean_myriel [smile]: Take your time looking. The iron is honest, even if the shapes are a touch livelier than country folk like.
shop
-> menu

~ work
jean_myriel [weary]: Left my old mountain town by night because the elders called my scrollwork wicked. Here, so long as I mend their ploughshares, nobody asks why my candlesticks have thorns.
-> menu

~ village
jean_myriel [sly]: Half the town wants silver charms against the moor, and the other half wantspadlocks against their neighbours. Good business for a smith either way.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: The quench-barrel beside the anvil smells faintly of rust and old salt, not plain rainwater.
jean_myriel [sly]: Sharp eyes. I learned my tempering among the Crimson Rose, where we quenched good steel in a drop of willing blood, though I stick to pig's blood here.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
jean_myriel [smile]: Just mountain slag in the ore, friend. Gives the steel a rosy tint when the fire runs hot.
-> menu
